{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"e50dfa0eb0ff7f5c6248f946909638e9676a0928adf607e42e9a4e7ace830867","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_d92379b83b5e55a3c3e241a75431185a7dada3e3d80ffb8d7f5533a8b8cc0808","overall_assessment":"The paper is well-organized and clearly written, with a logical progression from theoretical analysis to experimental validation. The mathematical notation is consistent and well-defined, and the tables are readable and informative. The main clarity weakness is the lack of a dedicated algorithmic summary for the training procedure, which requires the reader to synthesize the method from the text and equations.","paper_id":"Hyx0slrFvH","paper_identity_sha256":"e15c3401b39cd7ace8f35546126ddb946da0bc8275b99ff9b77192436c339437","prompt_identity_sha256":"bc418526e95f22871aac03a2d5aea89bb9d0b67be0de0e5d128914f51947cde1","raw_response_sha256":"23622404f8bf8d463b804a8961d9f823552177203b54f80cf7d3202afadb0cb6","request_identity_sha256":"43a29eb12992544dde1463fea6e38d588c057c46a07d3f2942398f8a930ed6d8","reviewer_identity_sha256":"c1cd7c7fdd4a2cbeb45c2f21af982ad0f30bffae8ae148e3eba36479685cf360","role":"CLAR","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"178c5cb135ddce163b9677e54a73087ac2367e52029a04f03c808e2c9ef7d14c","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-007","SRC-018","SRC-033"],"review_text":"The paper is well-structured, with a clear narrative that moves from the motivation for mixed-precision quantization to the theoretical analysis of parametrizations and finally to experimental results. The notation is introduced early and used consistently throughout. However, the presentation of the training algorithm could be improved. The method involves a specific procedure for handling discrete constraints (rounding in the forward pass, STE in the backward pass) and a penalty-based optimization framework. While these components are described in the text, a dedicated algorithm box or pseudocode summarizing the full training loop would make the method more self-contained and easier to reproduce. Additionally, the term 'differentiable quantization (DQ)' is introduced in Section 2.1 but is not formally defined as a distinct algorithmic step, which could be clarified by explicitly stating that DQ refers to the specific parametrization and gradient estimation strategy proposed.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-WRT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-009","SRC-012","SRC-013","SRC-014","SRC-017"],"review_text":"The mathematical notation is clear and consistent. The paper defines the quantizer parameters and their relationships (e.g., q_max = (2^(b-1) - 1)d) explicitly, which is helpful for understanding the different parametrizations. The derivations of the gradients for the three cases (U1, U2, U3) are presented in a structured manner, and the key insight regarding the boundedness of the gradient norm for U3 is well-supported by the equations. The notation for the power-of-two quantization is also clearly defined. One minor point is that the transition from the continuous parameter space to the discrete constraints (e.g., rounding to the nearest power-of-two) is described in Section 2.2 but could be more formally integrated into the mathematical formulation of the optimization problem to avoid any ambiguity about the domain of the parameters during the gradient computation.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-NOT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-010","SRC-015","SRC-036","SRC-038"],"review_text":"The tables in the paper are readable and provide clear comparisons between different quantization schemes. Table 2 effectively summarizes the computational complexity and memory footprint for different layer types and quantization methods. Tables 3 and 4 present the experimental results in a structured way, allowing for easy comparison of the proposed method against baselines. The captions for Figures 1 and 2 are detailed and accurately describe the content of the figures, which is helpful for understanding the theoretical analysis. The caption for Figure 5 also provides sufficient context for the bitwidth assignment results. The textual descriptions of the figures are consistent with the data presented in the tables.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-FIG"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"3801f3d244f427834f6dbded45fde4503549718c99c68126c38e20826a6e34c6","paper_id":"Hyx0slrFvH","paper_ordinal":104,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"23622404f8bf8d463b804a8961d9f823552177203b54f80cf7d3202afadb0cb6","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"Hyx0slrFvH","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"de0f7956bdc5789ed01d937519a59a53e8d96e2c9ff41d90a9da7bb8ab1ab6c0","request_identity_sha256":"43a29eb12992544dde1463fea6e38d588c057c46a07d3f2942398f8a930ed6d8","role":"CLAR","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v5","usage":{"completion_tokens":818,"prompt_tokens":21996,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":22814},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"43a29eb12992544dde1463fea6e38d588c057c46a07d3f2942398f8a930ed6d8","role":"CLAR","role_ordinal":1,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v4"}